<article class="env-situation" id="08PA">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08PA">Situation <span data-tag="08PA">21.38.3</span>.</a> Let $(\mathcal{D}, \mathcal{O}_\mathcal {D})$ be a ringed site. Let $u : \mathcal{C}' \to \mathcal{C}$ be a $1$-morphism of fibred categories over $\mathcal{D}$ (Categories, Definition <a href="/tag/02XP" data-tag="02XP">4.33.9</a>). Endow $\mathcal{C}$ and $\mathcal{C}'$ with their inherited topologies (Stacks, Definition <a href="/tag/06NV" data-tag="06NV">8.10.2</a>) and let $\pi : \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C}) \to \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{D})$, $\pi ' : \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C}') \to \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{D})$, and $g : \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C}') \to \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$ be the corresponding morphisms of topoi (Stacks, Lemma <a href="/tag/06NW" data-tag="06NW">8.10.3</a>). Set $\mathcal{O}_\mathcal {C} = \pi ^{-1}\mathcal{O}_\mathcal {D}$ and $\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{C}'} = (\pi ')^{-1}\mathcal{O}_\mathcal {D}$. Observe that $g^{-1}\mathcal{O}_\mathcal {C} = \mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{C}'}$ so that </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ (\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C}'), \mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{C}'}) \ar[rd]_{\pi '} \ar[rr]_ g &  &  (\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C}), \mathcal{O}_\mathcal {C}) \ar[ld]^\pi \\  &  (\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{D}), \mathcal{O}_\mathcal {D}) }  \]
</div>
  <p> is a commutative diagram of morphisms of ringed topoi. </p>
</article>